use std
into text_test.amni

```amni
import os;
import dm;
import html;
import rtf;
import textfmt;
import eml;
```

`put(text const byte[:])` writes text with `os::write_stdout` line by line: a carriage byte (13) at the end of a line is not written, every line that is empty (after that) is written as a single period instead, and every line ends with a newline (a last line without a newline gets one; an empty text writes nothing). Every multi-line print of this program goes through `put`, so the expected output below has no empty lines.

`show(name const byte[:], which int)` reads the file "tests/fixtures/" followed by name with `os::read_file` (printing "missing" and returning when it cannot be read), calls `dm::dm_reset(kind, unit)` where kind and unit are "html" and "section" for which 1, "rtf" and "section" for 2, "text" and "section" for 3, "csv" and "sheet" for 4, 5 and 6 (and 8), "json" and "section" for 7, "eml" and "part" for 9, then calls the reader chosen by which: 1 `html::ht_read`, 2 `rtf::rt_read`, 3 `textfmt::tx_text`, 4 `textfmt::tx_csv` with delimiter 0, 5 `textfmt::tx_csv` with delimiter 9, 6 is unused, 7 `textfmt::tx_json`, 9 `eml::em_read`. It prints a line "== " and the name, then the Markdown from `dm::dm_markdown` (written with `put`), then one line "meta " plus key, an equals sign and value for each line of `dm::dm_meta` (the key and value are separated by the tab byte 9 there), then one line "warn " plus the line for each line of `dm::dm_warn`, and when the reader returned false one line "reader returned false".

`main()` calls `show` for these files in this order: "page.html" with 1, "memo.rtf" with 2, "escapes.rtf" with 2, "notes.md" with 3, "quoted.csv" with 4, "semi.csv" with 4, "table.tsv" with 5, "data.json" with 7, "records.json" with 7, "lines.jsonl" with 7, "mail.eml" with 9, "fwd.eml" with 9, "nested.eml" with 9. Then it prints a line "== page.html text-only", reads "tests/fixtures/page.html" and prints `html::ht_text_only` of it with `put`. Then it prints a line "== mail.eml attachments" and for every attachment i of `eml::em_att_count` (after reading mail.eml again with `dm::dm_reset("eml", "part")` and `eml::em_read`) prints "att ", i, a space, the name from `eml::em_att_name`, a space, the type from `eml::em_att_type`, a space, the byte length of `eml::em_att_data` and then the data itself on the following lines with `put`. Finally it calls `negatives`.

`negatives()` prints a line "== negatives" and then, for each of these pairs of reader and file, one line made of the reader name, " on ", the file name, ": " and the word "true" or "false" for what the reader returned (the file under "tests/fixtures/" is read with `os::read_file` and `dm::dm_reset("text", "section")` is called before each reader): `html::ht_read` on "notes.md", `rtf::rt_read` on "notes.md", `eml::em_read` on "notes.md", `eml::em_read` on "page.html", `textfmt::tx_json` on "notes.md".

